From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Paes <78096758+paesdan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] settings: Bluetooth and printers without Python

blueman and system-config-printer are Python programs, so a distribution
without Python has neither, and Shell Settings' Bluetooth and Printers rows
(and the Control Panel's Bluetooth lever) open nothing. After them, in the
order they are preferred, come Runink River's own launchers: river-bluetooth
(bluetuith, a Go TUI, in a terminal) and river-printers (CUPS's own pages,
http://localhost:631, in the default browser). A machine with blueman or
system-config-printer still gets those.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Paes <78096758+paesdan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
